+## 2026-10-24 review-f4bbc5c710b4b80e — size-shortcut repair
+
+The issued 2.0.1 distribution made every holed object size 8 or 10 and every
+solid distractor size 3 or 4. Consequently the executable rival “recolor every
+component of size at least 8” matched ordinary generated labels without
+examining holes. The old `self_check` also required only a global enclosed zero;
+it did not require a solid contrast component.
+
+Version 2.0.2 keeps the intended rule and canonical Racket authority unchanged.
+It deterministically includes an eight-cell 3×3 holed ring and a nine-cell
+filled 3×3 solid in every ordinary draw. The remaining shapes, colors, positions,
+and counts continue to vary. `self_check` now classifies same-color components
+using border-reachable background and rejects lessons missing either a holed
+component or a solid distractor.
+
+Evidence:
+
+- `tests/test_learnability.py` was written against the old source first. The
+  size-contrast test failed on old draws with holes `[8]` and solids `[3,4]`;
+  the all-holed self-check regression also failed because no solid contrast was
+  required. Both tests now pass.
+- Fresh staged task tests: 2/2 passed in
+  `checks/b31e765ef780-tests/result.json`.
+- `counterexamples/review-f4bbc5c710b4b80e/reproduce.py` replays the old and
+  repaired sources through protected Racket. The size rival matches both old
+  demonstrations, then differs from the repaired query in 18 cells. Six Racket
+  evaluations passed; the exact report is `large-component-shortcut.json`.
+- `counterexamples/review-f4bbc5c710b4b80e/sweep.py` checked 4,096 deterministic
+  ordinary draws over four difficulty values, 128 seeds, and eight sample
+  indices. All 4,096 passed `self_check` and contained a solid larger than a
+  holed object; see `sweep.json`.
+
+These finite checks refute the explicit size-threshold rival and validate the
+new contrast invariant. They do not eliminate every possible conditional rule,
+grant owner approval, or admit training data.
